# Testing Standards

## Naming
- `describe` block: the component or function name
- `it` / `test` block: `"should [behavior] when [condition]"`
- Test file: co-located with the component, same name + `.test.tsx`

## Coverage requirements
- All public functions in `src/lib/` must have unit tests
- All reducer actions must have tests for the happy path and the error/empty case
- UI components: test behavior (interactions, state changes), not implementation details

## Tools
- Unit tests: [YOUR TEST RUNNER — e.g. Vitest or Jest]
- Component tests: [YOUR COMPONENT TESTING APPROACH — e.g. React Testing Library]
- Do not use `describe.only` or `it.only` in committed code
- Do not mock modules unless the real module is impractical (e.g. network, native APIs)

## Assertions
- Prefer user-visible assertions: `getByRole`, `getByText`, `getByLabelText`
- Avoid: `getByTestId` unless no semantic alternative exists
- Avoid: snapshot tests for logic — prefer explicit assertions
